course: dictionary
lesson: 15502
title: What is a subcontinent?
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A continent is a huge piece of land, like Asia or Europe. A subcontinent is a smaller part of a continent that is separate in some way, often by mountains, sea or history. The word is made of two parts: sub, meaning under or part of, and continent. So a subcontinent is a part of a continent.
explain: «The Indian subcontinent is shut off from the rest of Asia by high mountains and the sea.» The clues are shut off, high mountains and the sea. They tell you the land is separate, even though it is still joined to Asia. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A piece of a continent that is set apart fits well.
explain: When people say «the subcontinent», they usually mean South Asia: India, Pakistan, Bangladesh, Nepal, Bhutan, Sri Lanka and often the Maldives. Geographers, historians and newspapers all use the word this way, so you will meet it in many lessons.
fact: A subcontinent is a very large piece of land that is part of a continent but is separate in some way.
fact: «The subcontinent» usually means South Asia, the land south of the Himalayas.
fact: The Indian subcontinent sits on its own tectonic plate, which crashed into Asia and pushed up the Himalayas.
fact: In 1947, the British Raj ended and India was divided in a event called partition.
fact: Check a new word by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «The Indian subcontinent is a large piece of land» still makes sense.
exercise: «Ravi lives in India, and his cousin lives in Nepal, both on the same subcontinent.» What is a subcontinent? | A country with its own king | *A very large piece of land that is part of a continent but is separate in some way | A small island in the sea | Japan and Korea
exercise: Which of these countries is part of the Indian subcontinent? | *Bangladesh | Egypt | Brazil | Japan
exercise: «The subcontinent is a large piece of land.» Find and copy one word that means a part of a continent. | river | village | *subcontinent | ocean
test: What happened when the Indian subcontinent crashed into Asia? | It split into two continents | It became an island | It sank into the sea | *It pushed up the Himalayas
test: In 1947 the British Raj ended and India was divided. What is this division called? | Pollination | Migration | Eruption | *Partition
exam: Why is India called part of a subcontinent rather than a whole continent? | *Because it is part of Asia but is separated from the rest of it by mountains and sea | Because it is a very small island in the ocean | Because it has no people living there | Because it is in Europe
